Engine: the ordnance in flight, "CMSL" (open fix 55).

STATUS: APPLIED 30 September 2026 by work order 194 (Part B; reserved by
work order 193) — orion2re f506bc6c on orionlayer-local (before: 9b7dcba0), this
file's diff byte for byte (index lines included). Required by
tools/version_check.py since work order 194.

It was applied, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_combat_ordnance.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert f506bc6c` or `patch -R -p1`,
and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    Missiles, torpedoes and fighters live in MOX::_missile (300 x
    s_missile, 0x1A bytes, sizes.h asserts it); none of it was serialized,
    and a missile's target (target_unit_idx) is what a client needs to show
    the threat and to aim anti-missile fire. Block "CMSL", written after
    CMBT while open fix 52's gate is up: version, battle serial, the record
    size, the number of live entries (type above 0, the test
    COMBINIT::Tactical_Combat_ uses), and each as int16 index + the struct
    as it is — the index is what _missile_field[] and a missile's target
    refer to. The "hit radii" 193 listed are not a stored value; they are
    computed per shot from positions both blocks carry.

    Only reads. An engine without OrionLayer behaves exactly as before. One
    marker, `OrionLayer, open fix 55.`, on the block's first comment line.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 3afad020..2c0b688e 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -1489,6 +1489,35 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
         }
         WriteBytes(buf, legal, sizeof(legal));
     }
+
+    // 20. The ordnance in flight: "CMSL", written ONLY while a battle is live,
+    //     after CMBT. OrionLayer, open fix 55.
+    //
+    //     Missiles, torpedoes and fighters live in MOX::_missile (300 x
+    //     s_missile, 0x1A bytes each — sizes.h asserts it); an entry is live
+    //     while its type is above 0 (the loop in COMBINIT::Tactical_Combat_).
+    //     Each live entry as the struct holds it, with its index — the index
+    //     is what _missile_field[] and a missile's target refer to.
+    if (g_combat_live && MOX::_missile != nullptr) {
+        int16_t live = 0;
+        for (int i = 0; i < 300; i++) {
+            if (MOX::_missile[i].type > 0) ++live;
+        }
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'C');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'M');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'S');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'L');
+        Write8(buf, 1);                                   // block version
+        Write16(buf, (int16_t)g_combat_serial);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)sizeof(s_missile));
+        Write16(buf, live);
+        for (int16_t i = 0; i < 300; i++) {
+            if (MOX::_missile[i].type > 0) {
+                Write16(buf, i);
+                WriteBytes(buf, &MOX::_missile[i], sizeof(s_missile));
+            }
+        }
+    }
 }
 
